cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "Error-Sensitive Alignment Bounds for Affine-Line Decoding: A Lean-Verified Refinement"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Ngo
    given-names: Nam Khanh
    affiliation: "Beethoven Capital (independent research initiative)"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-6013-7308"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "YYYY-MM-DD"  # set at release
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/OWNER/REPO"  # set at release
abstract: >-
  Lean 4 formalization, on top of ArkLib, of an error-sensitive threshold for deriving
  affine-line mutual correlated agreement from line decodability: max(floor(delta n) + 2, 3)
  aligned challenges instead of n + 1, when n < |F|, and the resulting bound
  ((delta n + 2) t + 3 t^3) / |F| for folded Reed-Solomon codes.
keywords:
  - Reed-Solomon codes
  - proximity gaps
  - mutual correlated agreement
  - line decoding
  - Lean 4
  - formal verification
